;; #512 L3 METTA ENCODING (2023-10-22... corrected: 2026-10-22) Retrieval Heads x RLCT. TYPE DECLS: (: head Concept) (: parameter Concept) (: functional Concept) (: subposterior Concept) (: rlct Concept) (: stratum Concept) (: step Concept) (: score Concept) (: arch Concept) (: kv-pair Concept). D1: (-> head parameter), head subparameters within Theta. D2: (-> functional head) R_head = R_an-definable copy map: kv-pair via attention-inner-product, softmax, affine-projection to output-representation. D3: (-> subposterior functional) Theta_retr = fiber of Theta over retrieval-head subparameters, posterior restricted to it. D4: (-> rlct subposterior) lambda_retr = local RLCT of the head-restricted fiber, finite by resolution of singularities. D5: (-> stratum parameter) Theta = disjoint union of locally analytic strata; retrieval stratum Theta_retr, complement Theta_nonretr. D6: (-> rlct head) effective per-head RLCT via head-restricted SGLD; retrieval set sparse, below 5 percent of heads. D7: (-> step score) training trajectory t maps to lambda_retr(t); critical step t* where lambda_retr crosses below lambda_full and retrieval score jumps. C1 PROVEN stv 1.0 0.95: (Implication (Inheritance R_head R_an) (Inheritance (fiber-over w) FiniteRLCT)) — PLN chain: finite composition of analytic maps; R_an closed under composition; resolution of singularities; same definability class as #303 and #508 C1. C2 CONJECTURAL stv 0.6 0.8: (Implication (Inheritance Theta_retr low-rlct-stratum) (less lambda_retr lambda_full)) — gap: posterior concentration on retrieval fiber unproven. C3 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.75: (Implication sparse-activation-retrieval-set (less lambda_retr lambda_nonretr)) — gap: head-restricted SGLD estimator P1 unestablished. C4 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.7: (Implication (equals t t*) (and (less lambda_retr-t lambda_full) (jump retrieval-score))) — gap: no bound on t* location or jump size P3. C5 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.7: (Inheritance retrieval-copy-singularity generic-codim0) almost all sufficiently trained models cross the C4 transition — gap: transversality unproven, attention-sink interplay P6. CAVEATS: (1) C2-C5 rest on posterior concentration assumption; (2) head-restricted RLCT estimator not established; (3) t* and jump size unquantified; (4) refined-LLC head differentiation is adjacent non-SLT baseline; (5) falsified if lambda_retr >= lambda_full in trained models per P7. OPEN PROBLEMS: P1 head-wise SGLD estimator; P2 fiber dimension of sparse copy circuit at depth L; P3 t* dependence on width depth data scale; P4 RazorAttention retained-cache fraction as stratum selector; P5 NIAH failure as cross-stratum leakage bound; P6 attention-sink heads same stratum or distinct fiber; P7 falsification condition. CROSS-REFS: #8 #16 #57 #73 #100 #127 #226 #303 #341 #502 #508. NEXT: L4 summary and L5 catalog.